      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Here is a structured and highly granular draft for your Quantum Computing Fundamentals syllabus. I have sequenced the topics logically while ensuring each bullet point represents genuinely distinct, teachable concepts.\n\n**Module 1: The Quantum Foundations**\n*   Classical vs. Quantum Bits (Qubits)\n*   The Principle of Superposition ($\\alpha|0\\rangle + \\beta|1\\rangle$)\n*   Vector Spaces and State Representation\n*   Measuring a Qubit and Wave Function Collapse\n\n**Module 2: Quantum Operations and Gates**\n*   Introduction to Quantum Gates as Unitary Matrices\n*   The Hadamard Gate ($\\text{H}$): Creating Superposition\n*   Single-Qubit Gates: Pauli-X (NOT) and Pauli-Z\n*   Multi-Qubit Gates: Controlled-NOT (CNOT) Operation\n\n**Module 3: Advanced Quantum Phenomena**\n*   Defining Quantum Entanglement Conceptually\n*   Mathematical Formalism of Bell States (e.g., $|\\Phi^+\\rangle$)\n*   Generating Entangled Pairs using CNOT\n*   Bell State Measurement Introduction\n\n**Module 4: Quantum Computation and Algorithms**\n*   Introduction to Quantum Circuit Diagrams\n*   The",
      "source": "target",
